================================================================================
The eBPF programs are GPL-2.0-only
================================================================================

File: crates/lidlesseye-ebpf/bpf/profile.bpf.c
License: GNU General Public License, version 2.0 (see LICENSE-BPF)

Reason: the Linux kernel refuses to load a BPF program that calls GPL-only
helpers unless the program declares a GPL-compatible license string. LidlessEye
uses `bpf_get_stackid` (perf_event and kprobe stack capture) and
`bpf_get_ns_current_pid_tgid` (PID namespace translation); both are marked
`gpl_only` in the kernel. The object therefore carries `SEC("license") = "GPL"`.

Scope: the BPF object is a program that is loaded into the kernel, not a
library that is linked against this crate or against any user-space code. The
kernel's own licensing rule ("GPL and explicit license compatible") applies to
the loaded program; it does not propagate to the Rust processes that load and
read from it. This is the same split used by bpftrace, parca-agent and the
OpenTelemetry eBPF profiler, all of which ship GPL-2.0 eBPF programs alongside
permissively licensed user-space code.

If you build LidlessEye with `LIDLESSEYE_BUILD_BPF=0` and supply your own
object, only that object's license applies to it.

